    "setting": "Indiana University School of Medicine (IUSM) is a dynamic blend of rigor, collaboration, and community. As one of the largest medical schools in the United States, IUSM spans nine campuses across Indiana, each with its own unique character but united by a commitment to excellence in education, research, and patient care. Whether medical students are in the urban settings of Indianapolis, Evansville, Fort Wayne and Gary or pursuing the rural education track of Terre Haute or prefer the traditional college campus setting of Bloomington, South Bend, West Lafayette and Muncie, they benefit from the same high-quality MD curriculum \u2014 with the special amenities and opportunities of each location.",
    "housing": "On-campus housing is limited, but there is an abundance of available housing within minutes of campus.",
    "supportSystems": null,
    "supportSystemsForDisabilities": "https://medicine.iu.edu/education/md/student-support/",
    "wellnessPrograms": "https://medicine.iu.edu/md/student-support/health-wellness",
    "campusCulture": "At the heart of the IUSM culture is a strong sense of teamwork. IUSM medical students often work closely with their peers, professors, and mentors in a collaborative environment. Group study sessions, peer-led review groups, and interdisciplinary interactions are integral to the learning experience. The medical school emphasizes a team-based approach to patient care and medical education, with students encouraged to engage with faculty and fellow students in a way that fosters mutual respect and collective problem-solving. The school\u2019s mission to broadly serve communities, both locally and globally. Many students at IUSM are passionate about health and wellness equity, actively engage in outreach and advocacy efforts to improve healthcare access for underserved populations. The school\u2019s community service initiatives\u2014whether through free clinics, health fairs, or global health programs\u2014are vital parts of the student experience, reinforcing a sense of purpose and responsibility.\n",
    "transportationDriverLicense": "Required",
    "transportationVehicle": "Required",
    "transportationAdditionalInfo": "IU School of Medicine requires learners to have access to reliable transportation across training sites. Medical students are responsible for understanding all site transportation requirements and making appropriate plans before the beginning of an educational experience.",
    "additionalSupportProgrameName": ""
  },
